<Project>

  <!-- Why this file exists: MSBuild reads Platform from the environment, and a solution build
       then demands a solution configuration for whatever it found — "Release|x64" for a shell
       that exported Platform=x64, which vcvarsall.bat does and some tooling inherits. This
       solution declares only the default configurations, so restore, build, test, pack and
       format all die with MSB4126 before a single project is loaded, on a machine where
       nothing is wrong with the checkout.

       An assignment here settles it, because an environment variable loses to a property set
       in a file while a command-line -p: wins over both. So an ambient Platform no longer
       decides how this solution builds, and an explicit -p:Platform=x64 still gets the honest
       MSB4126 it deserves: this solution really does not declare that configuration.

       Only solution builds import this file, so a project built directly is untouched. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <Platform>Any CPU</Platform>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
